11. The conditions referred to in paragraph 10(b) are that the person
was:
(a) a British citizen;
(b) a close relative of a British citizen;
(c) a national of a member state of the European Union or the
European Economic Area;
(d) a person who had a right to be in the United Kingdom by
virtue of being a family member of a national of a member
state of the European Union or the
European Economic Area;
(e) a national of a State party to the Council of Europe
Convention on the Compensation of Victims of Violent
Crimes (CETS No. 116, 1983);
(f) a member of the armed forces; or
(g) an accompanying close relative of a member of the armed
forces.

